      "Exact current MethodDef object, matching method entry, owned direct CALL instruction, unique instruction addresses and actual x64 Win64 PE header.",
      "Only executable native targets without metadata candidates, method registration or export identity. No method name or arithmetic identity is guessed.",
      "At most the existing default total 24 instruction states across the entire CFG, not per arm; both conditional paths must prove the same Single/Double scalar first use. Identical rejoins are deduplicated; backward/self edges, external or missing/mid-instruction targets decline.",
      "Exact legacy whole-XMM copies propagate aliases; direct calls remove volatile aliases and preserve only Win64 XMM6..15 scalar low lanes. Any ambiguous RAX use before a later call, indirect flow or unproved exit declines.",
      "Implicit vector reads, packed/high-lane/bitcast or untyped memory-escape reads do not prove scalar precision. Alias writes kill the fact, with exact legacy self-XOR treated as overwrite rather than old-bit consumption.",
      "No counted symbolic-register reads, input casts, helper replacement, high-lane inference, old linear-proof changes or expression-cap increases. Aggregate/address/overlap, RBP, interface-sret and scalar-home guards remain unchanged."
    ]
